Let's check the .env variable name. The .env read was blocked (it's an env file). The user said "i will provide the backend url in the .env file". So I need to pick a var name, e.g. `VITE_API_BASE_URL`. I can't read .env but I can check .gitignore/diff. Maybe I should check if there's already something in .env via git diff? It's blocked regardless. Let me check whether other services use an env var already (e.g., appointmentService or a api client).

Let me search for import.meta.env usage.

Also check AuthForm1.jsx / AuthShell1.jsx (duplicates, changed files). And check git status to see what's changed.

Let me also look at the AuthForm flow: after registration it shows feedback with a link to login. The user wants: after register → directed to login view. So navigate to `/${role}/login` instead of just showing a link. After login → patient dashboard (already handled by getAuthenticatedDestination for role patient).

