{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p12-3527493a","text":"FormField supports `as="textarea"` but no select. I need a gender select. Options:
- Add `as="select"` support to FormField with an `options` prop (small addition, reusable, matches project conventions).
- Or render a native select inline in AuthForm with its own markup/classes.

Adding select support to FormField is cleaner and consistent. FormField supports `as='textarea'`; adding select with `options` prop is a natural extension. But careful: `controlProps` includes `type`, `autoComplete`, etc. For select, we'd render `<select {...controlProps}>` with options; `type` isn't a valid attr for select but React would warn. Also password toggle not relevant. Also dir would be fine.

Also, the label uses `pg-form-field__input-wrap` div with dir. For a select, put inside that wrap so styling matches? The CSS likely styles `.pg-form-field__input-wrap input, textarea` etc. Let me check FormField.css to see selectors so a select gets input styling.

