**What changed**

- [apiAuthAdapter.js](src/services/auth/apiAuthAdapter.js) (new) — POSTs to `/api/Auth/register/patient` and `/api/Auth/login` with `Content-Type: application/json`, a 15 s timeout, and maps responses: 200 register → success, 200 login → authenticated, 401/403 → "email or password is incorrect", 400/409 → field errors taken from the ASP.NET `errors` object (backend keys `FullName`/`PhoneNumber`/`Email`/… are mapped back to form fields), 429 → rate-limited, 5xx → unavailable, network/timeout → connection error.
- [session.js](src/services/auth/session.js) (new) — after a successful login the response is persisted in `localStorage` under `physioguide-session` as `{ token, user, authenticatedAt }`, with `loadSession` / `clearSession` available for the dashboard and a future logout. The token is looked up under `token`, `accessToken`, `access_token`, `jwt`, `idToken`, `authToken`.
- [authService.js](src/services/authService.js) — reads **`VITE_API_BASE_URL`** from `.env` and uses the live adapter for patients; without it, development falls back to the existing mock adapter and production reports "unavailable". Centers still use the mock adapter since no center endpoint was given.
- [AuthForm.jsx](src/components/auth/AuthForm.jsx) — successful registration now navigates to `/${role}/login` (replacing history) and shows "Your account has been created. Sign in to continue."; login still navigates to `/patient/dashboard`. Gender was added as a required select on patient signup (Male / Female, with a "Select gender" placeholder) per your choice.
- [authValidation.js](src/utils/authValidation.js), [FormField.jsx](src/components/shared/FormField/FormField.jsx), [en.js](src/locales/en.js) / [ar.js](src/locales/ar.js) — `gender` required for patient registration and included in the payload, generic `as="select"` support on FormField, and the new EN/AR labels.

**Put this in `.env`** (then restart `npm run dev`):

```
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend-host
```

